<title>USA: FSA qualifies eight muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies eight muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Piggott School District No 52, Ark., $1.105 million construction bonds.</p>
<p>--South Bend Central School District, Ind., $43.2 million bonds.</p>
<p>--Massachusetts Bay Transportation Authority, $200 million bonds.</p>
<p>--Tollgate Drain, Mich., $4.075 million bonds.  </p>
<p>--Somers Point, N.J., $1.7 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Deschutes County, Ore., $25.395 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Chester Water Authority, Pa., $9.765 million water revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--Chester County, S.C., $3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
